    "question": {
      "dom_id": "question-177650",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times \\{i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,0.5]\\times \\{0.5\\}=\\{(k,0.5)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,0.5]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0,0.5)$ to the point $(0.5,0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14167512/assets/7587daeaea45c5ef3449ecb676133c60bbedb7819308783bac835f3ae9c6883c.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times \\{i\\}=\\{(k,i)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(0,i)$ to the point $(i,i).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14167512/assets/b926204a3d58b25889f1c79dd0f65c1ea990c67bc88e869004396a77970e8dd4.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14167512/assets/4a81de1a698eedf6a636d66b68a7c62efa69d1d026a961ae97ab5ecc2ef9828d.png)",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Incorrect",
      "html": "<div id=\"question-177650\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">1.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/4387#13320\">Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"177650\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Let <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D43C TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2282\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom space=\"4\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c211D TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>⊂</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em; margin-left: -0.024em;\"><mjx-m